CORE gcc-only
constant.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
GCC's `a ? : b` constant-folds in constant contexts (aligned attribute, array
dimension, static assertion, enum value, bit-field width, case label), as used
by the Linux kernel's cache-line alignment macros.  gcc-only for the aligned
attribute.
